comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-23T13:57:18.042Z","harness:claude-code","Scope addition from the sixth Codex pass on PR #1772 (2026-11-23, P3, not reproduced here): schema add-field treats an explicit cliFlag that normalizes to nothing ('--') as omitted and silently drops a whitespace-only alias (normalizeAddFieldInput in src/core/schema/fields-file.ts), so the command succeeds with the default flag or without the requested alias, while the inline settings writer refuses the same spelling with schema_field_flag_invalid. Decide whether add-field should refuse an explicitly supplied empty spelling the same way; the same pass raised the duplicate inline definition and negated mutation flag cases again, both already in this item.\n"
  "2026-11-23T14:42:07.644Z","harness:claude-code","Two P3 additions from the seventh Codex pass on PR #1772 (2026-11-23, not reproduced here). (1) A field whose key is help but whose flag is another spelling (help-topic) is refused with schema_field_option_collision, because the key is compared with every built-in option including the implicit --help; the help option never supplies a parsed help value to the field reader, so only the flag and aliases should be compared with --help and -h, while the key check stays for built-ins that do supply parsed values. (2) runRegisteredCommandForTest builds the SDK through sdkFactory before output-control admission runs, so a factory sees global.outputLimit undefined for options { '--output-limit': '1' } while the handler sees '1', and the factory also runs for an invocation admission then refuses; resolve admission and the effective global controls before constructing the SDK.\n"
  "2026-11-23T14:53:24.124Z","harness:claude-code","Partly delivered in PR #1772 after CodeRabbit raised the same cases on c089f0d39 (2026-11-23): the harness now folds a negated boolean spelling of a mutation option (--no-add, no-add, noAdd with a boolean value) onto its base key as the normalizer applies it, so the negated-mutation case of this item is closed; and the SDK factory is built after admission, so it sees the resolved controls and never runs for a refused invocation (the second P3 above). Still open here: the duplicate inline field that becomes effective, the explicit empty add-field spelling, and the help key exemption.\n"
  "2026-11-23T15:33:43.810Z","harness:claude-code","Correction to the earlier note (2026-11-23): the negated-mutation fix in PR #1772 follows the option normalizer's rule (dashed no-<name> spellings of a declared boolean only), so it covers the declared --stdin case this item named. An undeclared native mutation key negated by a caller (for example --no-add on comments with no extension declaration) is passed through unchanged by the normalizer as well, so it is not a harness-native divergence.\n"
  "2026-11-23T17:22:03.728Z","harness:claude-code","Two harness-only additions from the final Codex pass on PR #1772 (2026-11-23, after merge as a5e8b5d3a; reported as reproduced by Codex, not re-run here). (1) annotationPositionalMutationOptions (src/sdk/read-output-contracts.ts) checks the command path before resolving it, so a harness call with command 'item comments' (or item notes / item learnings), args [id, text] and an output control runs the handler; native dispatch resolves the operation first and refuses. Resolve the path with the same resolver validateReadOutputOptions uses before the positional check. (2) The harness negation fold (negatedDeclaredBooleanKey and booleanToken in src/sdk/testing.ts) accepts only literal true/false and the long negated spelling, while the option normalizer also accepts 0/1 and case-insensitive trimmed tokens and a negation through a declared short alias; reuse the normalizer's spelling and boolean rules for admission. Both extend this item's harness-admission scope.\n"
  "2026-11-27T03:32:40.314Z","harness:claude-code","Fix (2026-11-27, branch fix/field-admission-diagnostics) for the five residual cases recorded here. (1) Settings writer: assertChangedSchemaFieldsAvailable (src/sdk/extension-command-context.ts) now also judges, per key, the definition the registry will read (the last resolvable entry) whenever it differs from the previously effective one, so a proposal that removes the winning duplicate and leaves an exact stored copy of an earlier shadowing one is refused with schema_field_option_collision; restating both stored entries still passes. (2) add-field and profile apply/lint: resolveAddFieldFlagSpellingDefects takes the supplied spellings, so an explicit --cli-flag or --alias that normalizes to nothing is refused with schema_field_flag_invalid (profile lint: field_flag_invalid) instead of being read as omitted or dropped. Through the SDK transport a whitespace-only cliFlag string is treated as omitted before it reaches add-field; filed separately. (3) Help key: resolveCommandCollisions judges a key spelled differently from every flag without the implicit --help option, because help exits before any handler reads a parsed value; key help with --cli-flag help-topic registers, stores values under help and leaves pm create --help working, while help as a flag or alias is still refused. (4) annotationPositionalMutationOptions resolves the command path with resolvePmHistoryOperation first, so a harness handler on item comments with positional text and an output control is refused like native dispatch. (5) The harness negation fold now calls resolveNegatedDeclaredBooleanOption (src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts), which runs the normalizer's own resolveNegatedBooleanSpelling over its spelling index, so 0/1, any case and spacing, and a negation through a declared short alias (no-S) count; a value the normalizer refuses is left for normalization to refuse. Specs: harness-parity, settings-field-admission and field-flag-spellings; with src reverted to main the four new cases fail."
  "2026-11-27T04:28:32.965Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 1 (2026-11-27) on e02d401c0, verified and fixed: the settings writer compared effective definitions over the inline list only, while the registry reads the fields file after it, so exposing an earlier shadowing inline entry was refused even when a file-backed definition of the same key stayed effective. assertChangedSchemaFieldsAvailable now appends the fields-file definitions (readFieldsFileDefinitions, current and proposed fields path) to both sides before choosing the effective definition per key; a spec covers the masked case."
  "2026-11-27T04:40:03.123Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 2 (2026-11-27) on 9de3e2c90, verified and fixed: (1) the settings writer returned early when the proposed inline list was empty, so a proposal that cleared it and pointed schema.files.fields at a file with a shadowing definition was never judged; the early return is gone, and the fields-file overlay is compared on both sides. (2) The harness negation fold treated an empty negated list as a mutation; an empty list is zero occurrences, as normalization delivers it, so resolveNegatedDeclaredBooleanOption yields nothing for it."
  "2026-11-27T04:49:47.846Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 3 (2026-11-27) on 518645ca9: fixed: the harness negation fold now treats a negated list whose entries normalization drops (blank or nullish only) as zero occurrences, so it no longer refuses it as a mutation; a list with a kept entry is still a mutation. Deferred to a follow-up: judging against the hydrated registry when the current schema fails to hydrate."
  "2026-11-27T04:57:09.381Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 4 (2026-11-27) on ef9ce2877, verified and fixed: the empty-negation check now calls the normalizer's own hasLooseListEntries on the inverted value for list and repeatable declarations, so a CSV value that keeps no entry once split (' , ') counts as zero occurrences too, instead of a hand-written per-entry blank check."
  "2026-11-27T05:34:24.512Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 6 (2026-11-27) on 3a88e434a, verified and fixed: when a file switch made a masked inline entry effective, the writer judged the proposal's normalized copy, which had already lost a blank alias that the stored entry keeps on disk, so the entry became effective without the empty-spelling refusal. The writer now judges the raw stored entry that resolves the same way, which is the spelling that stays on disk; a spec covers the unmasking switch."
  "2026-11-27T05:48:06.023Z","harness:claude-code","Greptile review on PR 1790 (P1, 2026-11-27), verified and fixed: the round 6 lookup replaced the winning definition with any stored inline entry that resolves the same way, even when the winner came from the fields file, so a clean file definition was refused because of a masked inline entry, and a file definition with a blank alias passed when the inline entry was clean. The effective map now records each definition's source; only an inline winner is judged by its stored spelling, and a file-backed winner is judged as the file holds it. Spec cases cover both directions."
